JH <no@email> wrote:
> Pardon me if this is the wrong place to ask, but here's the situation.  My
> brother and I play nethack on separate machines on our home network.  I was
> trying to think of a way to share bones files between the two computers.  My
> first idea was a simple batch file that would  copy the bones from a shared
> folder before playing, and copy them back after playing.

You should be able to create a folder to hold the bones on
one of the machines. Share that folder, then map a drive 
letter to that share on each machine and set
BONESDIR to point to it in defaults.nh on both machines.

You can share a common score file too, by setting SCOREDIR
in defaults.nh.

